## Temporary solution
We can still debug through VSCode but Chrome DevTool.
Hopefully the PR will be merged soon.

1. Create `./.vscode/launch.json`
2. Launch it from VSCode debug console.


![image](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/assets/14261588/586eff2e-b35a-4f2a-8a4c-2ca983a9803f)

`./.vscode/launch.json`
```json
{
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "Debug server-side",
      "type": "node-terminal",
      "request": "launch",
      "command": "pnpm dev", // or yarn dev or npm dev
      "cwd": "${workspaceFolder}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Debug client-side",
      "type": "chrome",
      "request": "launch",
      "url": "http://localhost:3000",
      "cwd": "${workspaceFolder}"
    },
  ]
}
```
`./package.json`
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "next dev"
  }
}
```
